Subject: [PATCH 01418/11171] [conductor] Pre-gate block: RFT TRAIN (Phase B
 part 2; gated on the corpus being ready). SYNCHRONOUS single-window
 LoRA-finetune of Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B (headroom rung) on the THREE arms from
 exp4088 -- Arm A RFT-CORRECT, Arm B RFT-ABLATION, Arm C gold-SFT -- with
 IDENTICAL hyperparameters/seed per arm (the ONLY difference is the corpus
 LABEL). Train SYNCHRONOUSLY (NOT background-detach -- the .377/.373-.375
 fabrication root cause); print per-epoch progress; checkpoint per epoch to
 STABLE per-arm paths so a 2nd window RESUMES (accumulate-across-milestones).
 A sub-1B LoRA finetune fits one ~75-min window. Prioritize Arm A + Arm B (the
 load-bearing ablation contrast) over Arm C if the window is tight.
 MiniCPM5-1B strong rung only if the window allows.

1 of 1 gate(s) failed; first failure: exp4088-verifier-reward-rft-corpus-build.runner_ready (actual=False == expected=True)

